from pathlib import Path
path = Path('docs/rag_workflow_v1.md')
append = """
## AF. Consistency cleanup
Canonical terminology ensures every section refers to the same enums and states:\n- **Modes:** `rewrite`, `apply_package`, `feedback`, `manual_review` (see sections Y/Z). All retries, controllers, and docs should reference this enum. Any older term should be mapped to one of these four.\n- **Intents:** use human-friendly strings such as `apply_linkedin`, `revise_cv`, `collect_feedback`, `start_manual_review`. Mentioned intents should always be lower-case, dash-separated, and documented in the request schema (section Y).\n- **Fallback reasons:** standard enum values are `none`, `missing_cover_letter`, `unsupported_claim`, `rewrite_no_op`, `token_budget`, `validator_schema_fail`. Section K, F, and O now reference this canonical set; do not invent alternate names (e.g., “coverage_failure” should map to `rewrite_no_op` or `unsupported_claim` as appropriate).\n- **Validator failure reasons:** canonical enum set is `none`, `validator_schema_fail`, `validator_evidence_fail`, `constraint_violation`, `coverage_low`. Use these everywhere validators are evaluated or logged (sections G, R, H).\n- **State names:** use the list from section S (`received`, `analyzed`, `evidence_mapped`, `planned`, `generated`, `validated`, `retrying`, `fallback_generated`, `manual_review`, `persisted`, `failed`). Any transition log must use one of these names exactly.\n- **Error taxonomy:** the canonical tags described in section H (`parse_error`, `retrieval_low_confidence`, `routing_misfire`, `rewrite_no_op`, `missing_cover_letter`, `unsupported_claim`, `validator_schema_fail`, `validator_evidence_fail`) should be the only codes emitted in logs/alerts.\nAll future documentation or code comments should map synonyms back to these canonical names before use.\n\n## AG. Global config / constants registry\n| Constant | Default | Purpose | Runtime configurable? |\n|----------|---------|---------|----------------------|\n| `RETRIEVAL_WEIGHT_SEMANTIC` | `0.55` | Semantic score weight in hybrid formula (section D) | Yes (env/config) |\n| `RETRIEVAL_WEIGHT_KEYWORD` | `0.30` | Keyword weight | Yes |\n| `RETRIEVAL_WEIGHT_METADATA` | `0.15` | Metadata weight | Yes |\n| `TOP_K` | `12` | Number of candidates retrieved | Yes |\n| `RERANK_TOP_N` | `3` | Candidates reranked | Yes |\n| `RAG_THRESHOLD` | `0.72` | Minimum total score for RAG path | Yes |\n| `FALLBACK_THRESHOLD` | `0.55` | Score below this triggers insufficient evidence path | Yes |\n| `DIFF_THRESHOLD` | `0.20` | Minimum normalized diff ratio to count as enhancement (section C) | Yes |\n| `COVERAGE_IMPROVEMENT_THRESHOLD` | `0.15` | Minimum coverage delta for must-have requirements (section C+U) | Yes |\n| `MAX_RETRIES` | `2` | Max retries before fallback (section L/U) | Yes |\n| `TIMEOUT_QUERY_MS` | `2000` | Query processor timeout | Yes |\n| `TIMEOUT_RETRIEVER_MS` | `3000` | Retriever timeout | Yes |\n| `TIMEOUT_RERANKER_MS` | `2000` | Reranker timeout | Yes |\n| `TIMEOUT_GENERATOR_MS` | `12000` | Generator timeout | Yes |\n| `TIMEOUT_VALIDATOR_MS` | `5000` | Validator timeout | Yes |\n| `TOKEN_BUDGET_FIRST` | `2200` | Prompt budget first attempt | Yes |\n| `TOKEN_BUDGET_RETRY` | `1600` | Prompt budget retry | Yes |\n| `TOKEN_BUDGET_FALLBACK` | `800` | Fallback budget | Yes |\n| `MAX_JD_LENGTH` | `3500` | Pre-compression JD character limit (section M) | Yes |\n| `MAX_CV_LENGTH_TOKENS` | `7500` | CV token limit | Yes |\n| `BATCH_SIZE` | `32` | Evidence batching | Yes |\n| `DB_LOCK_RETRY_COUNT` | `5` | Retry attempts for SQLite locks (section AB) | Yes |\n| `RETAIN_LOG_DAYS` | `90` | Logs/manual review retention (section Z) | Yes |\nThese constants should live in a shared config module and be logged on startup so operators always know the thresholds the runtime is honoring.\n\n## AH. Canonical normalization spec\nEnsure hashing/diff detection is deterministic:\n- **Lowercase rules:** all text used for hashing or keyword matching is normalized to NFC lowercase before processing (`.casefold()` for Python).\n- **Whitespace normalization:** collapse all whitespace sequences (spaces/tabs/newlines) into a single space; trim leading/trailing whitespace.\n- **Punctuation stripping:** remove punctuation characters except for evidence-scoped markers (e.g., `cv_snip_12`); keep hyphenated tech names but strip trailing punctuation.\n- **Bullet normalization:** canonical bullets start with `- ` followed by normalized text; reorder bullet lists alphabetically before diff hashing to avoid order noise.\n- **Evidence ID handling:** evidence IDs stay attached (e.g., `cv_snip_12`); include them verbatim in hashes/diffs but exclude them from textual similarity scoring by isolating them before punctuation stripping.\n- **Markdown/JSON cleanup:** remove markdown tables, code fences, and JSON braces before hashing; convert them to plain sentences via simple regex (e.g., `` `code` `` ? `code`) and treat braces as separators.\n- **Rendering artifact exclusion:** skip docx/pdf metadata (headers/footers) when computing diffs; only the raw CV text portion is normalized and hashed.\n- **Token comparison:** before checking budgets, tokens are normalized via the same lowercase/whitespace rules, so repeated runs produce the same counts.\nApply these exact steps before generating `cv_hash`, `diff_ratio`, or comparing tokens for retries.\n\n## AI. Document rendering contract\n- **CV JSON ? DOCX/PDF mapping:** `cv_rewrite.summary` becomes the introduction section; `experience_bullets` are rendered as ordered bullet lists grouped by role. Each bullet includes referenced technologies + evidence IDs in parentheses. Section order: summary ? experience ? skills ? metrics/fit.\n- **Cover letter mapping:** `cover_letter.title` becomes the document heading; `cover_letter.body` is split into paragraphs, each rendered with the evidence IDs cited in footers when available.\n- **Filename conventions:** `cv_{job_post_id}_{request_id}.docx/.pdf` and `cover_letter_{job_post_id}_{request_id}.docx/.pdf` stored under `documents/{request_id}/`. JSON contract saved as `artifacts/{request_id}/rewrite_contract.json`.\n- **Fallback behavior:** when `fallback_reason != none`, rendered files include a red warning header “Fallback output: evidence limited” and metadata records `fallback_reason` plus `validator_failure_reason`.\n- **Missing cover letter before fallback:** validators must prevent rendering until fallback supplies a letter; if fallback also lacks evidence, generate a placeholder page referencing the missing requirement with the “fallback” banner, but still persist the JSON contract.\n- **Embedded metadata:** rendered files include YAML front matter containing `schema_version`, `prompt_version`, `retrieval_version`, `validator_version`, `threshold_version`, and `generation_timestamp` so downstream systems can trace which config created them.\nThese steps apply to both normal and fallback outputs, ensuring every artifact is tagged for auditability.\n\n## AJ. Reprocessing / migration policy\n- **Prompt version changes:** when `prompt_version` increments (new template), existing outputs remain readable, but any request referencing an older version must re-run through the new prompt if flagged by manual review; otherwise mark `legacy_prompt=true`.\n- **Schema version changes:** `schema_version` bumps require revalidation; new reader logic must accept both `schema_version` values but mark old artifacts as `needs_revalidate` in `job_detail_validations`.\n- **Retrieval version changes:** adjustments to weights or filters do not invalidate past artifacts, but metrics should store both `retrieval_version` and `retrieval_version_at_generation`; reranking-only changes may skip reprocessing.\n- **Validator version changes:** when validator rules update, run a lightweight revalidation pass during the next scheduled sync; if failures emerge, flag `validator_version_mismatch` and queue the artifact for manual review.\n- **Threshold version changes:** since thresholds affect coverage/diff checks, artifacts produced under old thresholds remain valid but are flagged `threshold_version_mismatch` and can be re-run optionally. No automatic regeneration occurs unless the difference is critical; manual review can decide.\n- Old artifacts keep their original version tags plus a `legacy` boolean for quick filtering. When new versions are in place, the system logs `"reprocessing_needed": true/false` and documents whether a full regeneration, validator re-run, or simple note is required.\n\n## AK. Expanded worked examples\n1. **Happy-path output JSON**\n   ```json\n   {\n     "jd_analysis": {...},\n     "evidence_map": [...],\n     "fit_assessment": {...},\n     "cv_rewrite": {\n       "summary": "Senior React engineer building offline apps.",\n       "experience_bullets": [\n         "Led React PWA offline sync using IndexedDB (evidence: cv_snip_12)."\n       ],\n       "skills_focus": ["React", "TypeScript", "PWA"]\n     },\n     "cover_letter": {"title": "Application for Sr. React PWA", "body": "Paragraphs..."},\n     "quality_checks": {\n       "cv_enhanced": true,\n       "cover_letter_present": true,\n       "unsupported_claims_found": [],\n       "generic_phrases_found": [],\n       "fallback_reason": "none",\n       "validator_failure_reason": "none",\n       "notes": []\n     },\n     "metadata": {"schema_version":"v1.0","prompt_version":"v1.4","threshold_version":"v2.0"}\n   }\n   ```\n2. **Unsupported-claim output JSON**\n   ```json\n   {\n     "quality_checks": {\n       "cv_enhanced": false,\n       "cover_letter_present": true,\n       "unsupported_claims_found": ["PWA resiliency"],\n       "generic_phrases_found": [],\n       "fallback_reason": "unsupported_claim",\n       "validator_failure_reason": "validator_evidence_fail",\n       "notes": ["Need manual review for PWA evidence"]\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n3. **State transition trace**\n   ```\n   received ? analyzed (intent classified) ? evidence_mapped ? planned ? generated (retry_count=0) ? retrying (rewrite_no_op) ? planned ? generated ? validated ? persisted\n   ```\n4. **Persistence records snapshot**\n   - `job_generated_artifact_sets`: stores JSON contract, `cv_hash`, `idempotency_key`.\n   - `job_generated_documents`: paths `documents/req123/cv_req123.docx`, hash entries, render timestamp.\n   - `job_detail_validations`: verification rows storing `validator_version`, `quality_checks`, `error_taxonomy`.\n   - `job_fit_scores`: score breakdown row with `score_semantic=0.82`, `token_budget_used=2150`, `latency_ms=10900`.\n   - `job_state_transitions`: entries for each state with reasons (e.g., `retry_reason=coverage_delta`).\n5. **Deterministic fallback cover letter**\n   ```\n   Title: "Fallback: React PWA Application"\n   Body:\n     Paragraph 1: cite `cv_snip_12` describing offline resilience.\n     Paragraph 2: reference the tooling requirement via `cv_snip_19`.\n     Paragraph 3: closing sentence referencing JD summary with evidence ID `cv_snip_7`.\n   ```\n   Use evidence only once per paragraph, omit paragraphs lacking evidence, and keep total length =600 tokens.\n\n## AL. Final closing review\nSelf-review checklist:\n- Terminology alignment: modes/intents/fallback reasons/validator errors/states now canonical (section AF).\n- Centralized constants: registry in section AG holds all thresholds.\n- Deterministic hashing/diff: section AH outlines normalization rules.\n- Rendering behavior: section AI maps JSON to documents.\n- Version change policy: section AJ defines artifact handling per version bump.\n- Concrete examples: section AK now contains happy-path, unsupported claim, state trace, persistence snapshot, fallback letter.\n\nRemaining minor risks: fallback cover-letter language might need tonality tweaks after user review, and normalization rules still rely on consistent evidence ID encoding to avoid hash clashes.\n"""
path.write_text(path.read_text(encoding='utf-8',errors='replace') + append, encoding='utf-8')
